#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059504 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb1afe82-86ba-5a15-9037-74717692ecb2" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To a Coefficients Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "836f2f1b-5dd4-5dba-81cc-eb9ffe7db8d1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4693" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/assets/627d12115d61ddfdedf9db08330269de2137a23abceada977d039e90e5b88675.png)\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_2 := R_2 +(- 4) \\cdot R_1$ on $A?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation $R_2:=R_2 + (-4) R_1$ means that we need to add $-4$ times the first row to the second row. \n\nCarrying out this row operation, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 12 & 13\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4+(-4)(1) & 2+(-4)(2) & -1+(-4)(3) \\\\ 7 & 12 & 13\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -13 \\\\ 7 & 12 & 13\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059505 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c27a3f3c-77c7-55e9-8714-1f24c4a48063" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To an Augmented Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "2ff0a6f5-f3b2-5b39-8b69-1a0c969548cf" :question/math-academy-id "e-4694" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $A,$ given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/assets/82729e1d34174d58f01547b58aa63db28ec68a4e1964ef5cd127a2167ed4a722.png) \n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2$ on $A?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2$ means that we need to swap the first and second rows.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059506 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "691b9107-a935-5965-b3ac-0f3a193ce9bd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Appropriate Row Operation To Transform One Matrix Into Another"}] :question/id #uuid "a24c9621-793b-5c60-9c47-2b452f0faa2b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4695" :question/problem "Which elementary row operation could transform the matrix $A$ into the matrix $B$, where \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/assets/56fd7e343edf6c26f36718a30f899af6c8eaf0cad5f6b07c90ffa93c19df6346.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the $1$st and the $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has been changed is the $2$nd row. \n\nNow, applying the operation $R_2:=R_2+1 \\cdot R_1,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 4+1\\cdot (-4) & 1+1\\cdot (-2) & 2+1\\cdot 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the transformation could be done by the operation \n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+1\\cdot R_1\n$$\n\nor simply\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+R_1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059507 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0464b51e-8568-521e-96a5-a65c04569c2a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Appropriate Row Operation To Transform a Given Entry to a Desired Value"}] :question/id #uuid "f8417bbc-b748-519b-a997-fbb4aed755eb" :question/math-academy-id "e-4696" :question/problem "Given that\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448/assets/59ee8e91d058e347238320a2bd5496630f33534564f67f901d2ddf89000f0108.png) which elementary row operation could make $a_{22}=0?$" :question/worked-solution "In the given matrix, we have $a_{22}=5$ and we want to perform an elementary row operation that makes $a_{22}=0.$\n\n- We *cannot* make $a_{22}=0$ by switching two rows, because there are no rows with $0$ as the second entry.\n\n- We *cannot* multiply the second row by $0,$ because we are only allowed to multiply rows by *nonzero* constants.\n\n- However, we *can* add a multiple of another row to the $2$nd row to make $a_{22}=0.$\n\nLooking at the first row, we see that $a_{12}=1.$ If we add $-5$ times this entry to $a_{22},$ we will get $a_{22}=0$ as desired. So, the elementary row operation that we need to use is\n\n$$\nR_2 := R_2 + (-5) \\cdot R_1.\n$$\n\nApplying this operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1+(-5)\\cdot 3 & 5+(-5)\\cdot 1 & 6+(-5)\\cdot (-2) \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -16 & 0 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the desired elemetary row operation is\n\n$$\nR_2 := R_2 + (-5) \\cdot R_1,\n$$\n\nor simply\n\n$$\nR_2 := R_2 -5 R_1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059886 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb1afe82-86ba-5a15-9037-74717692ecb2" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To a Coefficients Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5a9bba7-f581-5372-a873-0fc17a55fb02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & -9 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056037} {:answer/id #uuid "b9c177a1-6771-55e3-bd09-bf47def49ac2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 & 9 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056038} {:answer/id #uuid "0d1d8e7e-44fc-5700-9bdc-f19ade4437e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056039} {:answer/id #uuid "5f95897b-76c9-50f9-ba67-9a60ae42a4ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056040} {:answer/id #uuid "64489d72-05e0-5199-9ab5-2517bee16eda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64489d72-05e0-5199-9ab5-2517bee16eda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056041} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe11ff0e-55ca-57c1-896c-442215af5968" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056036}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "73199f2e-4821-5c88-b3d1-fc53d8677008" :question/math-academy-id "q-10248" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $M,$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1}$ on $M?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $3$ times the first row to the third row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3+(3)(-1) & -1+(3)(2) & 9+(3)(4)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 21\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371638 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb1afe82-86ba-5a15-9037-74717692ecb2" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To a Coefficients Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cdbf1ce9-bdb2-5641-8842-42c0ad947f79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 9 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371640} {:answer/id #uuid "eba5bb7c-ef7a-536f-9354-b7ebf0b8836e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ \\frac{7}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 1 \\\\ 6 & 9 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371641} {:answer/id #uuid "0ab0188c-377b-5a0a-b42b-1996dc6aec4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 18 & 27 & -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371642} {:answer/id #uuid "50691937-0cf2-5b0c-a8ab-540484bad112" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371643} {:answer/id #uuid "e0a68aea-6889-51c4-a9d3-7f82e04efe3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50691937-0cf2-5b0c-a8ab-540484bad112" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371643} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0ba1504-253d-53d4-ba4d-851cb63ff768" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371639}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "584e4edf-d789-5238-8f2e-9096e3047b75" :question/math-academy-id "q-130006" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 9 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}$ on $A?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}$ means that we need to multiply the third row of the matrix by $\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nMultiplying the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{3}$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 9 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 6 & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 9 & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371645 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb1afe82-86ba-5a15-9037-74717692ecb2" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To a Coefficients Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fd9b1f4-d74d-52a3-9aed-e6db9d178847" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ -14 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371647} {:answer/id #uuid "ed2a940f-0183-5b3a-ab68-061004f95a08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 30 & 11 & -20 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371648} {:answer/id #uuid "52a4e6b3-4a0b-5914-8f6b-15a262b1fdd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 28 & 15 & -23 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371649} {:answer/id #uuid "543a3da9-cb2d-5855-8f46-085de649bb5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ -5 & 9 & -11 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371650} {:answer/id #uuid "94b6491b-89a0-5970-a0b4-b54e305f7242" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 26 & 19 & -26 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed2a940f-0183-5b3a-ab68-061004f95a08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 30 & 11 & -20 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371648} :answer-field/id #uuid "09e5f06a-ba45-55fc-8900-093b4ca249e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371646}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d1a5db75-1b21-5cae-946a-8cdf4a8b6bd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-130010" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $C,$ given by\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $C?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $3$ times the first row to the second row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 1+(3)(9) & -3+(3)(6) & -2+(3)(-7) \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 28 & 15 & -23 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 28+(-1)(-2) & 15+(-1)(4) & -23+(-1)(-3) \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 30 & 11 & -20 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371652 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb1afe82-86ba-5a15-9037-74717692ecb2" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To a Coefficients Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ca40eae-df66-5f6a-87dd-8f16815ee5df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 8 & -9 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371654} {:answer/id #uuid "cc0aa180-ede5-59c1-bea1-77279f662065" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371655} {:answer/id #uuid "e07e6a4b-d6bd-5903-9a52-48bd6ef4fa63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371656} {:answer/id #uuid "b3d32e5b-6ac1-505f-b225-5ca92f02981b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371657} {:answer/id #uuid "0e262b5f-82de-5b6c-8441-88cbf39620f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371658}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e07e6a4b-d6bd-5903-9a52-48bd6ef4fa63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371656} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9a1323d-0461-562e-9c29-f84d040eb176" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371653}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0b7da60c-f61b-5a37-b863-88993cbe5b14" :question/math-academy-id "q-130064" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $C,$ given by\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $C?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $-2$ times the second row to the first row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $1$ times the second row to the third row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0+(-2)(5) & 4+(-2)(2) & 7+(-2)(1) \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(1)\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1+(1)(5) & 3+(1)(2) & 0+(1)(1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371659 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb1afe82-86ba-5a15-9037-74717692ecb2" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To a Coefficients Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cbe97298-a9ad-5a8c-9549-0a7462c53337" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371661} {:answer/id #uuid "0d3cbffa-c49e-548b-8267-e1335fa1ebf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -9 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371662} {:answer/id #uuid "ba7f311d-0a4c-5ca6-a8b4-911934dd0189" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371663} {:answer/id #uuid "0d387b9c-0fec-54b7-8508-66a8a6ad06b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -19 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371664} {:answer/id #uuid "69cf1326-842c-5956-983e-4497c6b2c46b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbe97298-a9ad-5a8c-9549-0a7462c53337" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371661} :answer-field/id #uuid "afbbf945-a9a2-509f-90f6-e9683eb7ed6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371660}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cfee5c37-280e-5558-a146-4e1e8d46522e" :question/math-academy-id "q-130065" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $C,$ given by\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $C?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+3{R}_{3} \\\\ {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $3$ times the third row to the first row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $5$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1+(3)(2) & 2+(3)(0) & 1+(3)(-1) \\\\ -9 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -9 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -9+(5)(2) & 0+(5)(0) & -4+(5)(-1) \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371666 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c27a3f3c-77c7-55e9-8714-1f24c4a48063" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To an Augmented Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d43b8365-16f7-503d-83bb-4a18510b2877" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 9 \\\\ -1 & -9 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371668} {:answer/id #uuid "e41b9691-4f2e-5b34-999e-53a4638a8993" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -9 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371669} {:answer/id #uuid "2dd37626-b219-5653-9b30-6ed54d3bb3d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -9 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 9 \\\\ 6 & 5 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371670} {:answer/id #uuid "9bf73389-fc62-5b99-8ccc-fa414dbf736e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & -9 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371671} {:answer/id #uuid "e8544bce-f337-50d4-ae5a-e63b72e7a667" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 9 \\\\ 6 & 5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & -9 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d43b8365-16f7-503d-83bb-4a18510b2877" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 9 \\\\ -1 & -9 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371668} :answer-field/id #uuid "57cae7f9-3380-56f5-8ba4-1fe22cdfd5d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371667}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9c233556-3933-5343-a26f-9f78347091e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-130070" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 9 \\\\ 6 & 5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & -9 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ on $A?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ means that we need to swap the first and second rows.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 9 \\\\ 6 & 5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & -9 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}6 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 9 \\\\ -1 & -9 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303759 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c27a3f3c-77c7-55e9-8714-1f24c4a48063" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To an Augmented Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a66fe5d-99c6-50a1-8dd0-2bfdf26188c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303761} {:answer/id #uuid "a680c5fd-f83d-5b29-9e4d-996bb9ba9e7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303762} {:answer/id #uuid "feb9bda7-c609-5e9e-94c2-c8e6e44d91f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 9 & -2 & 6 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 5 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303763} {:answer/id #uuid "497d59d9-ad3d-5e2b-bfe2-a86e8abe6dba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303764} {:answer/id #uuid "bf35f16a-1ebc-5434-a2f0-bf2b3606d964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ -10 & 9 & -7 & -1 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 5 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a680c5fd-f83d-5b29-9e4d-996bb9ba9e7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303762} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae95e35e-7214-5649-b004-be41d40c67a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303760}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "37f7576f-ad33-50dc-9b99-0070faaebd2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-130072" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $V,$ given by\n\n$$\nV=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 9 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 5 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $V?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\ {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}$ means that we need to swap the first and third rows.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 9 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 5 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 4+(-1)(-1) & 4+(-1)(9) & 6+(-1)(-2) & 7+(-1)(6) \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303766 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "691b9107-a935-5965-b3ac-0f3a193ce9bd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Appropriate Row Operation To Transform One Matrix Into Another"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c447dfa5-a9b0-5db1-8e6e-876bad94c896" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303768} {:answer/id #uuid "16c897ca-87fe-5d91-97f9-6100801f9421" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303769} {:answer/id #uuid "5a4528bb-cb33-53b2-9709-8f35d0caae11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303770} {:answer/id #uuid "6b3fe4fc-6591-5a01-9780-4712432f2e66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303771} {:answer/id #uuid "029ae91a-4117-50a8-9c95-82893d0d2163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{3}{10})\\cdot {R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c447dfa5-a9b0-5db1-8e6e-876bad94c896" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303768} :answer-field/id #uuid "862d9f74-d4be-5bf3-a22f-ffe0d62845dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303767}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f3d65526-4014-502b-a3c6-a6538d0c4e88" :question/math-academy-id "q-130087" :question/problem "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $A$ into the matrix $B$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 5 & -5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the $1$st and the $2$nd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $3$rd row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $3$rd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 5 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {R}_{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "691b9107-a935-5965-b3ac-0f3a193ce9bd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Appropriate Row Operation To Transform One Matrix Into Another"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "244ba311-6d39-5e7a-873d-7c1e694c8a69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303789} {:answer/id #uuid "3c2ed31e-51d8-533f-aeca-5d84abdd1017" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303790} {:answer/id #uuid "438b2e59-539c-5152-84a4-5b9d2165c1bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303791} {:answer/id #uuid "3fa3c56f-ec98-564e-bff4-9dcf54797632" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303792} {:answer/id #uuid "a524de75-edc9-57fe-9c17-dccb2d520e48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "244ba311-6d39-5e7a-873d-7c1e694c8a69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303789} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6810500-4627-5b65-9c93-028292400d77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303788}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "31819a12-f2d2-51e4-a7d4-6a1c6ab3a626" :question/math-academy-id "q-130103" :question/problem "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $X$ into the matrix $W$, where\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -5 & -10 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the $2$nd and the $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $1$st row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $1$st row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & -5 & -10 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =W.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303794 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0464b51e-8568-521e-96a5-a65c04569c2a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Appropriate Row Operation To Transform a Given Entry to a Desired Value"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "830db774-11d9-5543-86d7-d72bdeff5f44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303796} {:answer/id #uuid "3f0d434b-f426-5080-9579-dc0b8d528769" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303797} {:answer/id #uuid "5a3bb336-bfad-5097-8f8f-ea2834827bde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303798} {:answer/id #uuid "52e45cd7-b826-5cad-8a2f-37fd8328fb15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303799} {:answer/id #uuid "35678761-4fc2-5c45-96fd-1ed69862673c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303800}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "830db774-11d9-5543-86d7-d72bdeff5f44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303796} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae3e3992-dc29-5cb1-a022-4ced463aae3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303795}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "01083ad9-2ef8-55b5-a0c4-a85dc2bfe174" :question/math-academy-id "q-130283" :question/problem "Given that\n$X=[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 10 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$,\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes ${a}_{13}=0?$" :question/worked-solution "Of the given options, we consider the row operation \n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 10 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371673 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0464b51e-8568-521e-96a5-a65c04569c2a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Appropriate Row Operation To Transform a Given Entry to a Desired Value"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29859872-ca1d-5b32-b8cf-520273889fa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371675} {:answer/id #uuid "0811f7c8-e1cd-50a2-95d7-96d8022f6ef7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371676} {:answer/id #uuid "6a563480-0f24-5bdc-8699-a58232f13ef4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:=(-2){R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371677} {:answer/id #uuid "2308f9ff-a2eb-52b3-9520-3fbaf21fc8ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371678} {:answer/id #uuid "9f623627-ecb1-592b-bb09-ff50aa7588b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0811f7c8-e1cd-50a2-95d7-96d8022f6ef7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371676} :answer-field/id #uuid "86383cb1-d9e2-5cb3-89a5-5fc3ce282b88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371674}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0c4d4bd0-aa70-5c1e-b9e2-635a1c35ddda" :question/math-academy-id "q-130285" :question/problem "Given \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -9 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 8 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]$,\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes ${a}_{32}=0?$" :question/worked-solution "Of the given options, we consider the row operation \n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -9 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 8 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -9 & 1 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371680 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0464b51e-8568-521e-96a5-a65c04569c2a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Appropriate Row Operation To Transform a Given Entry to a Desired Value"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8dde2649-f3cc-527d-9874-10029abd8d51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}↔{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371682} {:answer/id #uuid "1be16eb3-67d5-594d-988e-42b9be095356" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371683} {:answer/id #uuid "617f5a56-9487-5144-82df-e4df54be3c7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371684} {:answer/id #uuid "299f6585-ec3b-507c-a253-f36c4843b453" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371685} {:answer/id #uuid "8464edac-bd39-532a-ba1a-d1bb2c565b86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371686}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "299f6585-ec3b-507c-a253-f36c4843b453" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371685} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e6c7936-5b69-585c-a673-c678490e0f12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "29d236e0-1878-5137-ba17-eb57f50fa729" :question/math-academy-id "q-20386" :question/problem "Given \n$D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]$,\n which of the following elementary row operations makes ${a}_{31}=0?$" :question/worked-solution "Of the given options, we consider the row operation \n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1}.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371687 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "691b9107-a935-5965-b3ac-0f3a193ce9bd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Appropriate Row Operation To Transform One Matrix Into Another"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59886eec-5b76-5272-81cc-d142ff776816" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371689} {:answer/id #uuid "3ed66a36-9c8d-580a-a249-73f97a945541" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371690} {:answer/id #uuid "bba9d503-04fd-5495-99de-6490a453477b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371691} {:answer/id #uuid "7ac79a0b-4c51-5040-8edd-8a0941cb3d16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371692} {:answer/id #uuid "37ef4a59-22e0-5882-8897-e02584f2673b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bba9d503-04fd-5495-99de-6490a453477b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371691} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1892170-7ed3-526b-81f1-ab8abb87f797" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371688}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d2a8dbb7-9603-524c-971f-27fd98667b24" :question/math-academy-id "q-20387" :question/problem "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $S$ into the matrix $T$, where\n\n$$\nS=[\\begin{aligned}60 & 0 & 120 \\\\ 20 & 0 & 40 \\\\ 15 & 0 & 30\\end{aligned}],\\,T=[\\begin{aligned}15 & 0 & 30 \\\\ 20 & 0 & 40 \\\\ 15 & 0 & 30\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the $2$nd and $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $1$st row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that changes the $1$st  row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =[\\begin{aligned}60 & 0 & 120 \\\\ 20 & 0 & 40 \\\\ 15 & 0 & 30\\end{aligned}] & \\,{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}15 & 0 & 30 \\\\ 20 & 0 & 40 \\\\ 15 & 0 & 30\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =T.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371694 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c27a3f3c-77c7-55e9-8714-1f24c4a48063" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To an Augmented Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "192dc6cd-78cd-5304-b7af-df3f1d214d93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371696} {:answer/id #uuid "e4df7cf2-aac7-553b-877e-6cb67d2a8fca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371697} {:answer/id #uuid "7e7c4fe3-ee5a-52f8-a31e-733c92511db7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371698} {:answer/id #uuid "5e453c45-0417-5b9b-8be2-1eb8139668e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371699} {:answer/id #uuid "641a07f6-019f-5c96-897c-12f9a1738625" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "641a07f6-019f-5c96-897c-12f9a1738625" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371700} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5a49d2a-631e-5d78-b09d-520420f129e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371695}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7e529998-60b8-53c0-bae5-50351fb55c46" :question/math-academy-id "q-72757" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}$ on $T?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $2$ times the first row to the second row. \n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2+(2)(1) & -2+(2)(3) & 1+(2)(2)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371701 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c27a3f3c-77c7-55e9-8714-1f24c4a48063" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To an Augmented Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5175a431-00e2-5855-9621-7201124c4e00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371703} {:answer/id #uuid "82b27b13-6f43-56cc-b68d-c90d3d58b619" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371704} {:answer/id #uuid "cc35c5fa-247f-5124-b5a6-f8f94585cd33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371705} {:answer/id #uuid "d340fbf3-5924-5ad6-a24b-580c36345a93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371706} {:answer/id #uuid "d7235c6d-1e3b-5b81-94d5-9c906e668fff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc35c5fa-247f-5124-b5a6-f8f94585cd33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371705} :answer-field/id #uuid "24f5c6a9-2126-504b-b81d-9e871487c69e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7bb79bc8-bcb7-5840-8ed7-f3bc7161c5d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-72763" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M,$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ on $M?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the first row to the third row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1+(-1)(1) & -1+(-1)(0) & 1+(-1)(2) & 2+(-1)(3)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371708 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c27a3f3c-77c7-55e9-8714-1f24c4a48063" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To an Augmented Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "065f0191-ea2f-591a-a214-9cb9533530fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371710} {:answer/id #uuid "17bef35b-c83e-50e7-bf46-93f38cbe163f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371711} {:answer/id #uuid "1b94abbc-c06b-59a7-b38a-e3e736cf9f3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371712} {:answer/id #uuid "20525e74-cfb6-554f-9f33-c5998b714fa7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371713} {:answer/id #uuid "af5b8fda-c1d1-5c20-84fe-18728c4df6e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371714}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17bef35b-c83e-50e7-bf46-93f38cbe163f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371711} :answer-field/id #uuid "44c980be-2f7a-5b48-bd77-aa5c9b59bfc4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371709}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2facacda-0611-5507-a35e-091ce7069bfa" :question/math-academy-id "q-72781" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $N,$ given by\n\n$$\nN=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ on $N?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $-2$ times the first row to the second row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2+(-2)(1) & 1+(-2)(-2) & 2+(-2)(1) & 3+(-2)(-1) \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371715 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "691b9107-a935-5965-b3ac-0f3a193ce9bd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Appropriate Row Operation To Transform One Matrix Into Another"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df865a4c-f091-5a19-908c-188da5ffe640" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371717} {:answer/id #uuid "57dcaddb-e17a-5319-8391-1bbfaa5e1746" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=2{R}_{3}+4{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371718} {:answer/id #uuid "51686c06-537b-5183-ad26-a8da2b4f161f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371719} {:answer/id #uuid "7ce6b170-3815-5197-874e-f691b9c0a607" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371720} {:answer/id #uuid "8c33d05c-8340-5f0c-84f4-7b580b4d86e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}↔{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ce6b170-3815-5197-874e-f691b9c0a607" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371720} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0d16a95-65f1-52c0-9345-aa9b08de7040" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371716}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "796dfdc4-dc11-5fb3-8b4d-d35b9831de3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-72850" :question/problem "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $U$ into the matrix $V$, where\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the $2$nd row is the same in both matrices. The only rows that have changed are the $1$st row and the $3$rd row.   \n\nBy considering the given row operations that change both the $1$st and the $3$rd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] & \\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =V.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371722 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "691b9107-a935-5965-b3ac-0f3a193ce9bd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Appropriate Row Operation To Transform One Matrix Into Another"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19f9e8f2-f823-52c8-84d1-ca4b330b8994" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371724} {:answer/id #uuid "f3e50a0a-cfdb-5337-8175-1ace643b47ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371725} {:answer/id #uuid "8b41bef5-0524-5407-a72f-b63576d2085c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371726} {:answer/id #uuid "6b5e353f-2098-5235-8784-050c2dabb80b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371727} {:answer/id #uuid "a0057d8d-f392-54e4-b18a-90d49217d312" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371728}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b41bef5-0524-5407-a72f-b63576d2085c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371726} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c24a5cb-d140-53b2-a14b-ea1b845c083e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371723}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0036de8b-5fff-5bbf-814a-73d67f190a9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-72854" :question/problem "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $X$ into the matrix $W$, where\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the $1$st and the $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $2$nd row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $2$nd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =W.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371729 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0464b51e-8568-521e-96a5-a65c04569c2a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Appropriate Row Operation To Transform a Given Entry to a Desired Value"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fcc24ab-b842-55f5-9aa5-a6c3447ebd61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:=(-1){R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371731} {:answer/id #uuid "1d88ecb9-c302-59a1-9893-becd727a2967" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371732} {:answer/id #uuid "6c278518-20f2-57df-8461-04ac38998bd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371733} {:answer/id #uuid "655f522a-a132-52e1-9ded-4ff6cf0c12d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}↔{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371734} {:answer/id #uuid "e48e34b9-1996-5a03-9337-29b7369721f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e48e34b9-1996-5a03-9337-29b7369721f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371735} :answer-field/id #uuid "29998fc5-5844-5bc5-b0d5-e8c190f510a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371730}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "98d5b2ef-e0f1-5947-9335-d5945e4a2ed8" :question/math-academy-id "q-72857" :question/problem "Given that\n$C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\,-4 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ 0 & \\,-1 & \\,4 \\\\ 2 & \\,2 & \\,1\\end{aligned}]$,\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes ${a}_{33}=0?$" :question/worked-solution "Of the given options, we consider the row operation    \n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\,-4 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ 0 & \\,-1 & \\,4 \\\\ 2 & \\,2 & \\,1\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\,-4 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ 0 & \\,-1 & \\,4 \\\\ 3 & \\,0 & \\,0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371736 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0464b51e-8568-521e-96a5-a65c04569c2a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Appropriate Row Operation To Transform a Given Entry to a Desired Value"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "acdcdc32-30b0-5cf3-b84a-32cf961bb989" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371738} {:answer/id #uuid "dfcad798-1082-582e-b7af-2eed6d8a92ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}↔{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371739} {:answer/id #uuid "3c67c01e-261d-53fa-9319-2b806a64688f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371740} {:answer/id #uuid "d08a9684-0f16-526a-afd0-e20491f6738b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371741} {:answer/id #uuid "ded10a0a-15c1-57c6-9d59-51ced5260b7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}↔{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371742}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acdcdc32-30b0-5cf3-b84a-32cf961bb989" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371738} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f53c1fa-6aaa-5a50-82a5-8993fe528b5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371737}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "56f3ee9a-749b-5ee8-a1d2-09a47e5716ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-72860" :question/problem "Given that\n$S=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]$,\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes ${a}_{33}=0?$" :question/worked-solution "Of the given options, we consider the row operation \n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1}={R}_{3}+(-3)\\cdot {R}_{1}\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is \n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3)\\cdot {R}_{1}\n$$\n\nor simply\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1}.\n$$"}]}
